---
// The public Sahyog Drive — Story 11b.1 (Task 3; AC1, AC2, AC3, AC4, AC5, AC6, AC7, AC9, AC10).
//
// ⭐⛔ READ THIS FIRST — THE TIER-LEAK LEG ON THIS SURFACE IS **OPERATIVE FROM ITS FIRST COMMIT**.
// `sahyogDriveSurfaceFieldIds(model)` returns a NON-EMPTY set, so `evaluateSnapshot` actually
// evaluates the leak rules here and a planted `authenticated_member`-tier or UNDECLARED field at
// `public` FAILS a run that previously passed. ⛔ A green scan over an armed-but-empty leg proves
// nothing, which is why this surface never had one.
//
// ⭐ WHAT THIS PAGE RENDERS: the drives this trust has run — Active (window closed, family not yet
// paid) and Archive (paid out) — one bounded page at a time, filterable by district, date and drive
// code, each row carrying the number of contributions CONFIRMED as money received.
// ⛔ EVERY value goes through `<MatrixField>`, so `getVisibility()` is the ONLY thing deciding what
// appears.
//
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ⭐ REMEMBRANCE, NOT ANALYTICS (AC5)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// This page exists so anyone can verify the trust actually moves money, and so a drive run in
// someone's memory stays on the public record. ⛔ It is NOT a leaderboard, NOT a scoreboard, and
// NOT a way to harvest who gave what.
// ⛔ PROHIBITED: contributor leaderboards · rankings ("top contributors", "supporter of the month")
// · gamification (badges, streaks, achievements) · social-performance metrics (most-supportive
// district, public scoreboards) · popularity metrics (most-viewed memorial, trending pools).
// ✅ ACCEPTABLE: legitimate trust verification · district/date historical research · accessibility
// · performance.
// ⭐ THE TEST: *"Does this serve remembrance, transparency or claim discoverability?"* If the honest
// answer is ENGAGEMENT, RANKING or SOCIAL PERFORMANCE, the proposal is REJECTED at design time.
// ⛔⛔ AND THE SORT ORDER IS NOT A RANKING — close/settle instant descending, ⛔ never by
// contribution count and ⛔ never by amount. ⭐ There is deliberately NO sortable column header
// here: "sort by contributions" is a leaderboard wearing a table affordance.
// (Also recorded in `lib/sahyog-render.ts` and the abuse-rules README.)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// ⭐⛔ CONSENT DECIDES WHETHER A ROW IS **NAMED**, ⛔ NEVER WHETHER IT **EXISTS**. A family that
// declines — or later withdraws — removes their relative's NAME. The drive still appears, with its
// code, its district, its date and its contribution count. ⇒ the index degrades PER-POOL, ⛔ never
// per-page. ⛔ And a withheld name renders NOTHING: no placeholder, no dash, no "withheld" marker —
// *an omission that announces itself is an ENUMERATION SIGNAL.*
//
// ⛔⛔ BUILT IS ⛔ NOT PUBLISHED. Counsel's DPDPA review of this exact subject is HELD
// (`2026-08-24-157` cl.3(a), returning 2026-09-07); Row 17's ≥2-trustee publication posture extends
// here via C-5 and this surface has ⛔ no ratification of its own; and the per-Pariwar switch is
// consulted on every request. ⛔ Nothing about this file being merged enables the surface anywhere.
// ⚠ Counsel HAS NOT REVIEWED this subject — ⛔ never write that counsel is not engaged, which has
// been false since 2026-06-21 (`2026-08-24-158`).
//
// ── ⛔ WHY THE DATA COMES OVER HTTP AND NOT FROM A LOCAL READ ────────────────────────────────
// D6(a), and `2026-08-20-143` cl.1 before it. Rendering a NAMED drive row needs a Tier-1 KYC
// decrypt (KMS deps), an anti-enumeration ceiling (a rate-limit store) and an abuse counter (the
// BYPASSRLS service pool). `apps/public` has NONE of the three, and ⛔ must not gain the first: the
// KEK is shared across EVERY Tier-1 field class. ⛔ Do not add a `withPublicScope` read here.
//
// House shape, mirroring `members.astro`: thin frontmatter, ALL display logic in the pure
// `lib/sahyog-render.ts`, explicit `namespace` on every `t()` call (⚠ `t()` defaults to `common`
// and THROWS on a miss — the `{{max}}` vs `{max}` defect that made `/members` throw on EVERY
// request at 11a.2 was exactly this shape, and no test caught it because every test bypassed `t()`).
import { formatCount, getLocale, isLocale, t } from '@twt/i18n';
import type { Locale } from '@twt/i18n';
import { passport } from '@twt/domain';

import MatrixField from '../components/MatrixField.astro';
import PublicShell from '../layouts/PublicShell.astro';
import { getDb } from '../lib/db.server.js';
import { visibilityOf } from '../lib/matrix.server.js';
// ⚠ `PUBLIC_PAGE_SIZE_MAX` is deliberately NOT imported. `/members` interpolates the cap into its
// rejection copy; this surface's rejection state is REJECTION-INVARIANT and says only "return to
// the first page", so naming the cap would tell a prober which bound it hit — the one thing that
// state is shaped to withhold. ⛔ The cap is still enforced, by `parsePageParams`, unchanged.
import { pageHref, parsePageParams } from '../lib/pagination.js';
import { ACTIVE_PARIWAR_ID } from '../lib/pariwar.server.js';
import {
  buildSahyogRejectionView,
  buildSahyogView,
  formatSahyogLiveAmount,
  formatSahyogTargetAmount,
  IST_OFFSET_MS,
  selectIndexLineVariant,
  splitSections,
  visibleSahyogColumns,
  type SahyogLabels,
} from '../lib/sahyog-render.js';
import { buildForwardedFor, fetchSahyogDrive } from '../lib/sahyog.server.js';

// ── Locale + branding (cache-safe: no session, no member state) ──────────────
const langParam = Astro.url.searchParams.get('lang');
const acceptLanguage = Astro.request.headers.get('accept-language') ?? undefined;
const db = getDb().db;
const passportRow = await passport.getPariwarPassportCached(db, ACTIVE_PARIWAR_ID);
const locale: Locale = isLocale(langParam)
  ? langParam
  : getLocale({ pariwarPassportLocale: passportRow?.localeDefault, acceptLanguage });
const trustName =
  (locale === 'hi'
    ? (passportRow?.displayNameHi ?? passportRow?.displayNameEn)
    : (passportRow?.displayNameEn ?? passportRow?.displayNameHi)) ?? 'Sahyog Drive';
const branding = passportRow?.brandingBundle ?? null;

// ⛔ NOTE THE ABSENCE: there is no `withPublicScope` member or pool read here, and there must not
// be one. The passport read above is branding, ⛔ not drive data.

// ⚠ EXPLICIT NAMESPACE ON EVERY CALL — `t()` defaults to `common` and THROWS on a miss.
const tr = (key: string, params?: Record<string, string | number>) =>
  t(key, params, { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-drive' });

// ⭐⭐ THE ONE SHARED STAGE VOCABULARY (`2026-09-04-193` cl.3, Story 11b.12 AC4). ⛔ The three stage
// names and their explanations live in `sahyog-shared` and ⛔ NOWHERE else — ⛔ do not re-add a
// `status.*` or a `section.*.help` key to `sahyog-drive.json`. ⚠ Two sources is exactly how
// *"Active"* came to mean two different things; the drive page and (at story E) the member app read
// these same keys.
const ts = (key: string) => t(key, undefined, { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' });

const labels: SahyogLabels = {
  pageTitle: tr('page.title'),
  pageIntro: tr('page.intro'),
  // ⭐ Story 11b.14 (AC1) — the LIVE section. ⚠⛔ Its heading and caption **COMPOSE** story B's
  // shared `stage.live` word with a section noun from `sahyog-drive.json`; ⛔ the WORD itself is
  // never restated there (`-193` cl.3, and that file's own `$comment` forbids it).
  tableCaptionLive: tr('table.caption.live', { stage: ts('stage.live') }),
  tableCaptionActive: tr('table.caption.active'),
  tableCaptionArchive: tr('table.caption.archive'),
  sectionLiveTitle: tr('section.live.title', { stage: ts('stage.live') }),
  sectionActiveTitle: tr('section.active.title'),
  sectionArchiveTitle: tr('section.archive.title'),
  columnName: tr('table.col.name'),
  columnPool: tr('table.col.pool'),
  // ⭐ Story 11b.10 — the drive-link column's header + its cell text + its per-row accessible name.
  columnOpen: tr('table.col.open'),
  viewDrive: tr('link.view_drive'),
  // ⚠ EXPLICIT NAMESPACE, and the drive CODE is interpolated — ⛔ never a person's name, which is
  // Tier-1, consent-gated and null for any unconsented family (the a11y name would then VANISH on
  // exactly the rows that still need one).
  driveLinkA11y: (poolCanonicalIdentifier: string) =>
    tr('link.view_drive_a11y', { code: poolCanonicalIdentifier }),
  columnLetter: tr('table.col.letter'),
  columnDistrict: tr('table.col.district'),
  columnDate: tr('table.col.date'),
  columnContributions: tr('table.col.contributions'),
  columnProgress: tr('table.col.progress'),
  // ⭐⭐ Story 11b.14 (AC7) — the RULED public label. ⛔ *"Account holder"* may ⛔ NOT be used
  // (`2026-09-04-190` cl.2, Trustee-ratified); `sahyog-copy.test.ts` asserts the resolved value.
  columnNominee: tr('table.col.nominee'),
  columnSummary: tr('table.col.summary'),
  columnOutcome: tr('table.col.outcome'),
  // ⭐⭐ STORY 11b.14 (AC3) — THE RULED LIVE-ROW SENTENCE, from the ONE shared source. ⛔ It is
  // Trustee-ratified copy (DR + KB, 2026-09-07) and is ⛔ never composed here.
  // ⚠⛔ THE NUMBER FORMS ARE RULED AND LIVE IN `sahyog-render.ts`, ⛔ not in this frontmatter —
  // a display decision written here would be untestable. ⭐ `formatSahyogLiveAmount` carries the
  // ₹10-lakh cut-off; `formatCount` carries *"For colleagues shows exact number"*.
  participationLine: (amountInr: number, contributorCount: number) =>
    t(
      'live_line',
      {
        amount: formatSahyogLiveAmount(amountInr, locale, 'live'),
        count: formatCount(contributorCount),
      },
      { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
    ),
  // ⭐⭐ STORY 11b.14 — THE RULED **ZERO-STATE** SENTENCE (`2026-09-07-206` cl.4). Trustee-ratified
  // copy (DR + KB, 2026-09-07) in BOTH languages; ⛔ never composed here, ⛔ never translated here.
  // ⛔⛔ THE VARIANT CHOICE IS THE SAFETY PROPERTY, ⛔ not a nicety: `t()` THROWS on an unsupplied
  // token, so resolving `zero_line.full` for a family whose name may not be published would 500
  // `/sahyog` for everyone. ⭐ `no_family` covers that TOTALLY ⇒ ⛔ there is no unrenderable case
  // here, and ⛔ this function never returns `null` (unlike `indexLine`, whose four variants are
  // ⛔ not total). ⛔ Do ⛔ not add a third variant at this site.
  zeroLine: (familyName: string | null) =>
    familyName === null
      ? t('zero_line.no_family', {}, { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' })
      : t('zero_line.full', { family_name: familyName }, { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' }),
  // ⭐ लक्ष्य. ⚠⛔ ITS AMOUNT FOLLOWS A **DIFFERENT** RULE — always lakh/crore, ⛔ never the cut-off.
  // ⛔ Do ⛔ not "align" the two: the divergence is the ruling.
  driveTargetLine: (targetInr: number) =>
    t(
      'drive_target',
      { amount: formatSahyogTargetAmount(targetInr, locale) },
      { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
    ),
  // ⭐⭐ STORY 11b.14 (AC7) — the ruled CLOSED · VERIFIED sentence, from 11b.12's shipped copy.
  // ⚠⛔ THE VARIANT IS CHOSEN IN `sahyog-render.ts`, ⛔ not here, and it returns `null` where ⛔ no
  // ratified variant fits ⇒ ⭐ this closure renders NOTHING rather than 500ing the page on a `t()`
  // throw. ⛔ Do ⛔ not "fix" a null by minting a fifth string — that is a Panel act.
  // ⚠ `{amount}` takes the EXACT form on these stages (*"For Closed, verified shows exact
  // figure"*), ⛔ never the lakh cut-off — `formatSahyogLiveAmount(..., 'closed')` is what says so.
  indexLine: (tokens) => {
    const variant = selectIndexLineVariant(tokens);
    if (variant === null) return null;
    const amount = formatSahyogLiveAmount(tokens.amountInr, locale, 'closed');
    // ⛔ `t()` THROWS on an unsupplied token, so each variant is given EXACTLY the params its
    // string names — ⛔ never a superset, which would hide a future copy edit that added one.
    //
    // ⚠⛔⛔ **THE `?? ''` FALLBACKS ARE GONE — ⭐ THEY INVERTED THE RULED FAILURE MODE** (Review
    // finding, 2026-09-07). ⭐ Each was DEAD today, because `selectIndexLineVariant` guarantees a
    // non-null value for every token the chosen variant names. ⚠ ⛔ But if that selector were ever
    // edited, `?? ''` would have converted a LOUD `t()` throw into a rendered sentence with a hole
    // in it — *"₹ 12,000 contributed by colleagues for , nominee of Late …"* — ⭐ which is exactly
    // the *"⛔ no partial sentence"* outcome `2026-09-07-205` cl.6 rules out.
    // ⇒ ⭐ an unexpectedly-absent token now returns `null` and the row renders **NOTHING**, the same
    // silence the selector itself returns. ⛔ Do ⛔ not reintroduce a string fallback here.
    if (variant === 'no_family') {
      if (tokens.nomineeName === null) return null;
      return t(
        'index_line.no_family',
        { amount, nominee_name: tokens.nomineeName },
        { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
      );
    }
    if (variant === 'no_nominee') {
      if (tokens.familyName === null || tokens.districtName === null) return null;
      return t(
        'index_line.no_nominee',
        {
          amount,
          family_name: tokens.familyName,
          district_name: tokens.districtName,
        },
        { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
      );
    }
    if (variant === 'no_district') {
      if (tokens.nomineeName === null || tokens.familyName === null) return null;
      return t(
        'index_line.no_district',
        {
          amount,
          nominee_name: tokens.nomineeName,
          family_name: tokens.familyName,
        },
        { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
      );
    }
    if (tokens.nomineeName === null || tokens.familyName === null || tokens.districtName === null) {
      return null;
    }
    return t(
      'index_line.full',
      {
        amount,
        nominee_name: tokens.nomineeName,
        family_name: tokens.familyName,
        district_name: tokens.districtName,
      },
      { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-shared' },
    );
  },
  districtUnknown: tr('value.district_unknown'),
  dateUnknown: tr('value.date_unknown'),
  // ⚠ D3 — the FIELD NAMES are historical and deliberately not renamed; their VALUES are the
  // ruled **Closed** / **Verified** words, read from the ONE shared source.
  statusLive: ts('stage.live'),
  statusActive: ts('stage.closed'),
  statusArchive: ts('stage.verified'),
  emptyTitle: tr('empty.title'),
  emptyBody: tr('empty.body'),
  emptyFilteredTitle: tr('empty.filtered.title'),
  emptyFilteredBody: tr('empty.filtered.body'),
  outageTitle: tr('outage.title'),
  outageBody: tr('outage.body'),
  pastEndTitle: tr('past_end.title'),
  pastEndBody: tr('past_end.body'),
  rejectedTitle: tr('rejected.title'),
  rejectedBody: tr('rejected.body'),
  paginationLabel: tr('pagination.label'),
  previousPage: tr('pagination.previous'),
  nextPage: tr('pagination.next'),
  // ⭐ THREE DISTINCT STRINGS, one per opaque outcome token — ⛔ and NONE of them compares to a
  // target, quotes a percentage, or names a shortfall. `classifyCycleOutcome` already quarantined
  // the numbers upstream; this is the second place that quarantine has to hold, because copy is
  // where a shortfall would actually surface. ⚠ `microcopy.yaml`'s `pool-reality-comparison` tone
  // rule bites `fell short` / `shortfall` / `\d+% of the target` / `लक्ष्य से कम` at PR time.
  outcomeFullyFunded: tr('outcome.fully_funded'),
  outcomeUnderFunded: tr('outcome.under_funded'),
  outcomePartial: tr('outcome.partial'),
  // ⚠ Interpolated THROUGH `t()`, ⛔ never by local string surgery — the 11a.2 `{{max}}` vs `{max}`
  // defect threw on EVERY request and no test caught it, because every test bypassed `t()`.
  contributionsCount: (count: number) => tr('value.contributions_count', { count }),
};

// ── FR-91 forced pagination (AC6) ───────────────────────────────────────────
// ⭐ `parsePageParams()` REUSED UNCHANGED — ⛔ do not write a second parser. ⛔ NO SILENT CLAMP: an
// over-cap or out-of-horizon request is REFUSED with a decidable reason.
// ⚠ THE ONLY THING ENFORCING FR-91 ON THIS SURFACE. Story 1.14's guard walks the live in-process
// swagger document and Astro routes emit none — ⛔ do not cite it as coverage here (it DOES cover
// the `apps/api` route behind this page, which is a different claim).
// ⭐⛔ AN UNRECOGNISED QUERY PARAMETER IS A REFUSAL (AC3), AND IT IS REFUSED **HERE** (Review
// finding, 2026-08-27). `parsePageParams` examines only `page`/`limit`, so anything else used to
// fall through unexamined and render a normal 200 — falsifying `buildSahyogRejectionView`'s own
// doc-block, which named `?format=csv` as producing byte-identical rejection output.
// ⚠ AND THE CACHE MAKES IT MORE THAN A CORRECTNESS NICK: this surface is `edge_cacheable`
// (`s-maxage=300`), so an arbitrary `?x=<n>` minted an UNBOUNDED space of distinct shared-cache
// keys, each a fresh origin miss re-serving Tier-1 PII into a new PoP entry.
// ⛔ `lang` is allowed: it is the locale selector `PublicShell` reads, ⛔ not a filter.
const SAHYOG_ALLOWED_QUERY_PARAMS = new Set([
  'page',
  'limit',
  'district',
  'closedFrom',
  'closedTo',
  'poolCode',
  'lang',
]);
const hasUnknownParam = [...Astro.url.searchParams.keys()].some(
  (k) => !SAHYOG_ALLOWED_QUERY_PARAMS.has(k),
);

// ⚠ THE ONLY THING ENFORCING FR-91 ON THIS SURFACE. Story 1.14's guard walks the live in-process
// swagger document and Astro routes emit none — ⛔ do not cite it as coverage here (it DOES cover
// the `apps/api` route behind this page, which is a different claim).
const paging = parsePageParams(Astro.url.searchParams);
// ⚠ REJECTION-INVARIANT: an unknown parameter produces the SAME byte-identical state as a bad
// `page`/`limit`, so a prober learns ⛔ nothing about which bound it hit.
const rejection = paging.ok && !hasUnknownParam ? null : buildSahyogRejectionView(labels);

// ── The three ruled filter dimensions (AC3, D2(a)) ──────────────────────────
// ⛔ THERE IS NO NAME FILTER, and its absence is the design: `member_kyc_profiles` carries no blind
// index and envelope encryption gives every name its own DEK, so the only way to answer one is to
// decrypt the whole roster per request — the exact amplification `DIRECTORY_DECRYPT_CONCURRENCY`
// exists to close. ⚠ Deferred on a `name_blind_index` substrate story, ⛔ not closed.
// ⚠ `?? undefined` alone does NOT catch an empty string — and a GET form submission with any
// field left blank sends that field as `field=` (present, empty), not omitted. Forwarding `''`
// trips the API's `.min(1)` validation on a perfectly ordinary "I only care about one filter"
// submission (Review finding, 2026-08-26). `|| undefined` treats blank the same as absent.
const districtFilter = Astro.url.searchParams.get('district') || undefined;
const closedFromFilter = Astro.url.searchParams.get('closedFrom') || undefined;
const closedToFilter = Astro.url.searchParams.get('closedTo') || undefined;
const poolCodeFilter = Astro.url.searchParams.get('poolCode') || undefined;
const isFiltered =
  districtFilter !== undefined ||
  closedFromFilter !== undefined ||
  closedToFilter !== undefined ||
  poolCodeFilter !== undefined;

// ── The drive read (AC1, AC8) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⚠ `<input type="date">` yields a bare `YYYY-MM-DD`, but the API's `closedFrom`/`closedTo` are
// `z.string().datetime()` — a full ISO timestamp is REQUIRED, and a bare date string fails that
// schema (Review finding, 2026-08-26). Widened to the inclusive day boundary in each direction so
// "closed on this day" reads naturally to a visitor picking a single date in either box.
// ⭐⛔ THE DAY BOUNDARY IS **IST**, ⛔ NOT UTC (Review finding, 2026-08-27). `formatClosedAt`
// renders in IST, so anchoring the filter to a UTC day put the two 5½ hours out of step: a drive
// closed 2026-08-02 01:00 IST DISPLAYED as `02-08-2026` and then did ⛔ not come back when the
// visitor filtered for 2 August — a date you can SEE but cannot FILTER FOR. ⛔ Do not change one
// of these without the other; `IST_OFFSET_MS` is exported from `sahyog-render.ts` so there is ⛔
// one definition, not two. India has no DST, so the fixed offset is exact.
const istDayStartIso = (day: string): string =>
  new Date(new Date(`${day}T00:00:00.000Z`).getTime() - IST_OFFSET_MS).toISOString();
const istDayEndIso = (day: string): string =>
  new Date(new Date(`${day}T23:59:59.999Z`).getTime() - IST_OFFSET_MS).toISOString();

const closedFromIso = closedFromFilter ? istDayStartIso(closedFromFilter) : undefined;
const closedToIso = closedToFilter ? istDayEndIso(closedToFilter) : undefined;

// ⚠ Gated on `rejection`, ⛔ not on `paging.ok` alone — a rejected request must cost NOTHING
// upstream. An unknown parameter is a refusal, so it must not reach the API hop either.
const drive =
  rejection === null && paging.ok
  ? await fetchSahyogDrive({
      page: paging.page,
      limit: paging.limit,
      district: districtFilter,
      closedFrom: closedFromIso,
      closedTo: closedToIso,
      poolCode: poolCodeFilter,
      // ⛔ `Astro.clientAddress` ONLY, via the REUSED `buildForwardedFor`. The inbound
      // `X-Forwarded-For` header is deliberately NOT read — it is caller-supplied, and `apps/api`'s
      // `trustProxy: true` keys on the LEFTMOST chain entry, so forwarding it hands the attacker
      // the rate-limit key AND a fresh abuse-counter window per request (`2026-08-21-145` cl.2).
      // ⛔ Do not "restore the full chain" without re-reading that ruling.
      forwardedFor: buildForwardedFor(Astro.clientAddress),
    })
  : null;

// ⭐ A 4xx FROM THE API IS AN INPUT REFUSAL, ⛔ NOT AN OUTAGE (Review finding, 2026-08-27;
// ✅ RULED AC7 GOVERNS, BigDev 2026-08-27). `fetchSahyogDrive` now distinguishes the two, and a
// `'rejected'` reason routes to the SAME rejection state a bad `page`/`limit` produces — so a
// visitor who typed a space into the District box is told their search could not be read, ⛔ not
// that the trust's systems are down. ⚠ AC8's "`ok:false` presented as an OUTAGE" means TRANSPORT
// FAILURE; ⛔ the two states are not interchangeable, and the first review pass patched two
// triggering inputs while leaving this collapse in place.
const apiRejected = drive !== null && !drive.ok && drive.reason === 'rejected';
const effectiveRejection = rejection ?? (apiRejected ? buildSahyogRejectionView(labels) : null);

const view =
  effectiveRejection === null && paging.ok
  ? buildSahyogView(paging, Astro.url.searchParams, labels, drive?.ok ? drive.data : null, {
      filtered: isFiltered,
    })
  : null;
const sections =
  view !== null ? splitSections(view) : { live: [], active: [], archive: [] };

// ⛔ A rejected request renders a 400-shaped state — ⛔ NOT a redirect to page 1, and ⛔ NOT a
// successful render of a different page than was asked for.
if (effectiveRejection !== null) Astro.response.status = effectiveRejection.status;

// ── Cache headers (AC7, D8(a)) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Declared `edge_cacheable` in public-vs-private-matrix.yaml, and the gate's cache-policy leg FAILS
// if this line and that declaration disagree.
//
// ⚠ ⭐ THE RULING STANDS; ITS ORIGINAL GROUND DOES NOT — RESTATED, ⛔ NOT QUIETLY PATCHED. D8(a) was
// argued as "the content is non-PII by construction, so it is cacheable by construction". D1(b) +
// D10 DESTROYED that: this page shared-caches Tier-1 PII — a deceased member's full legal name —
// behind a REVOCABLE consent. ⇒ the ruling now rests on the `/members` PRECEDENT (same class of
// field, same policy, re-decided at 11a.3 and kept, `2026-08-20-143`).
// ⛔ AND THE ACCEPTED COST IS LARGER THAN THAT ORIGINAL ARGUMENT SUPPOSED: a family's REVOCATION
// keeps being served from every warm PoP, PER PAGE NUMBER, for up to FIVE MINUTES. ⛔ Direct SQL is
// NOT the operational fallback.
// ⛔ AND THE COUNTER IS EDGE-BLIND: a cached hit never reaches the origin, so the origin-side rate
// limit and every abuse signal see only cache MISSES. Inert today (no edge in this repo; §5.8a) but
// a NAMED DEPENDENCY. ⛔ Do not "fix" it by making this surface `private_no_store` — that discards
// the edge for a public surface and was already REJECTED at 11a.3.
//
// ⭐ FOUR STATES, FOUR CACHE/STATUS PAIRS, AND THEY ARE ⛔ NOT INTERCHANGEABLE (Trap 7).
// `members.astro` keyed this branch on "not a rejection" alone, so the API-outage render, the
// visitor's own 429 and the kill-switched empty index ALL took the `edge_cacheable` arm at HTTP
// 200 — one transient blip pinned "could not be loaded" into a shared edge for five minutes.
// ⚠ `pastEnd` IS cacheable and deliberately so: it is a TRUE statement about a real index.
// ⛔ `apiUnavailable` is not: it is a statement about THIS request's luck.
//
// ⚠⛔⛔ **STORY 11b.14 (AC4) — HOW STALE A LIVE DRIVE'S METER CAN BE, STATED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT
// TO BE DISCOVERED.** FR-76 says the Active page is *"near-real-time during live alert"*. ⭐ This
// line is what bounds that: **up to FIVE MINUTES** behind at every warm PoP, and up to **one
// minute** in the visitor's own browser. ⇒ a Live row's bar, its confirmed count and its rupee
// figure are ⛔ **not** live to the second, and the ruled sentence's *"…and counting"* is what
// concedes it in the copy.
// ⛔⛔ **THE CACHE POLICY IS ⛔ UNCHANGED BY STORY 11b.14, AND ⛔ MUST NOT BE "TUNED" TO CLOSE THE
// GAP.** It is the same class of control as the rate tier (AC6), it was re-decided on the
// `/members` precedent (`2026-08-20-143`), and shortening it silently would trade a governed
// decision for a freshness preference. ⚠ The house reading of *"near-real-time"* is **polling,
// ⛔ never a push socket** (8.3 D6; 9.1) — ⭐ and polling ⛔ cannot outrun a shared cache, so a
// shorter poll interval would ⛔ not help either. ⇒ ⭐ the staleness is **ACCEPTED and STATED**.
//
// ⚠⛔ **AND ONE MORE CONSEQUENCE OF LISTING A LIVE DRIVE, STATED SO IT IS ⛔ NOT RE-OPENED IN
// REVIEW (Trap 5).** Listing a drive **PUBLISHES ITS ADDRESS** — `2026-09-04-186` records that a
// published link ends the work an unguessable address was doing, and `live` drives were the last
// case where it did full work, precisely because ⛔ nothing linked to them.
// ⭐⭐ **IT IS RULED, AND ITS STING IS ALREADY DRAWN.** Cite **`2026-09-05-200`**, ⛔ not `-186`
// alone: a Trustee ratification that landed AFTER this story's baseline answers the reachability
// question head-on — *"yes, a collecting drive's page should be reachable by the public"* (A1) and
// *"It doesn't change anything. Phone-app member should reach the page."* (A2), with its cl.4
// making the member-app path a **RATIFIED PROPERTY**, ⛔ not an implementation detail.
// ⭐ And `2026-09-04-190` cl.1 took the **banking coordinates off** the public drive page (story A),
// so what a published live address now reaches is the nominee's name and the drive facts —
// ⛔ **not account numbers**. ⇒ Trap 5's disposition is **STRONGER**, ⛔ not weaker. ⛔ Do not
// re-open it.
const cacheable = effectiveRejection === null && view !== null && !view.model.apiUnavailable;
if (cacheable) {
  Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=60, s-maxage=300');
  Astro.response.headers.set('Vary', 'Accept-Language');
} else {
  Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store');
}
// ⚠ AND THE STATUS TELLS THE TRUTH TOO. A page that says "could not be loaded" at 200 is a lie to
// every cache, crawler and uptime check in the path. 503 + `Retry-After` is the honest shape.
// ⛔ Not 500: the failure is upstream and transient, and this page rendered correctly.
if (effectiveRejection === null && view !== null && view.model.apiUnavailable) {
  Astro.response.status = 503;
  Astro.response.headers.set('Retry-After', '60');
}

const firstPageHref = pageHref('/sahyog', Astro.url.searchParams, 1);

// ⭐ RESOLVED ONCE PER RENDER, ⛔ not per row. The matrix cannot vary within a page, and asking
// `getVisibility()` per cell would be an N+1 on a constant. ⛔ `visibilityOf` is the ONLY thing
// consulted — no local tier comparison, no second viewer ceiling.
const driveColumns = visibleSahyogColumns(
  labels,
  (fieldId) => visibilityOf('sahyog-drive', fieldId, 'public').visible,
);

// ⭐ Story 11b.14 (Trap 4) — the LIVE section's columns. ⚠ It is the SAME function and the SAME
// matrix gate; ⛔ the only difference is that two columns which have no meaning before a drive
// closes are dropped **header and cells together**. ⛔ Do ⛔ not hand-build a second column list.
const liveDriveColumns = visibleSahyogColumns(
  labels,
  (fieldId) => visibilityOf('sahyog-drive', fieldId, 'public').visible,
  'live',
);

// ⭐⛔ `drive_status` IS THE ONE CLASSIFIED FIELD WITH NO `<MatrixField>` CELL, SO IT NEEDS THIS
// GUARD (Review finding, 2026-08-27).
//
// It is declared in `SAHYOG_DRIVE_ROW_FIELD_IDS` and in the matrix YAML — so the tier-leak leg
// counts it as governed — but it has ⛔ no entry in `visibleSahyogColumns`. Its value is disclosed
// STRUCTURALLY instead: by which of the three `<section>`s a row lands in (⚠ Story 11b.14 added the
// LIVE one), and by those sections'
// `<h2>` headings. ⇒ flipping `drive_status.tier` to `authenticated_member` in the YAML would
// suppress ⛔ NOTHING, every row would keep disclosing its status through placement, and the leak
// gate would stay GREEN because the field id is still declared.
//
// ⛔ This guard does NOT hide the sections — hiding them is a real design change (the Active /
// Archive split IS this page's structure) and inventing a silent fallback would be worse than the
// gap (⚠ Story 11b.14: the split is now Live / Closed / Verified, and the same reasoning holds).
// ⭐ What it does is make the inertness IMPOSSIBLE TO INTRODUCE QUIETLY: a matrix verdict this
// page cannot honour now FAILS THE RENDER instead of being ignored.
const driveStatusVisible = visibilityOf('sahyog-drive', 'drive_status', 'public').visible;
if (!driveStatusVisible) {
  throw new Error(
    '[sahyog.astro] the matrix suppresses `drive_status` for `sahyog-drive` at the `public` tier, ' +
      'but this page discloses it STRUCTURALLY — through the Active/Archive section split and its ' +
      'headings — and has no cell to suppress. Honouring that verdict requires removing the ' +
      'sectioned layout, not a config change. Restore the tier, or redesign the page deliberately.',
  );
}
